ange, block2=green\nSo clicking block2 from (O, W) goes to (O, N). This means block2 cycles: N -> W -> N -> W -> ...\nAnd the current state is (O, N).\nLet me map out the full state machine:\n- (W, N) --block1--> (O, N)\n- (O, N) --block1--> (W, N)\n- (W, N) --block2--> (O, W)\n- (O, W) --block2--> (O, N)\n- (O, N) --block2--> ??? (haven't tried)\n- (W, N) --block2--> (O, W) [confirmed]\nWait, from (O, W), clicking block2 goes to (O, N). So block2 cycles W -> N when block1 is orange.\nAnd from (W, N), clicking block2 goes to (O, W). So block2 cycles N -> W when block1 is white, but block1 also changes W -> O.\nHmm, this is getting complex. Let me think of it differently.\nActually, let me look at the current state: (O, N). I haven't tried clicking block2 from this state. Let me try that.\nAlso, I notice I haven't seen a (W, W) state yet. Let me think about how to reach it.\nFrom (O, N), if I click block1, I should get (W, N).\nFrom (O, N), if I click block2, what happens?\nLet me try clicking block2 from (O, N).", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": false}, {"label": "ASSISTANT", "content": "World model: State machine emerging: (W,N)<->(O,N) via block1 clicks. (W,N)->(O,W)->(O,N) via block2 clicks. Current state: (O,N).\nGoal model: Need to find (W,W) or other target state. Try clicking block2 from (O,N).\nPlan: Click block2 from current (O,N) state to see transition.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# Current state is (O, N). Click block2 to see what happens.\nresult = action([{'action': 'MOUSE', 'row': 36, 'col': 39}])\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\ncolors = [(n['color'], min([p[0] for p in n['boundary']])) for n in seg['nodes'] if n['pixels'] > 5 and n['color'] not in ['S', 'R']]\nprint(\"After click:\", colors)\nprint(\"Done:\", result.get('done'), result.get('level_completed'))\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"